Right. But that isn't the point I was trying to make (that the colnames 
would be something in particular). Instead, I was pointing out that the 
coefficients being estimated will be the same regardless, and the only 
difference is the order in the design matrix.

>
> > colnames(model.matrix(~phenotype+area))
>   [1] "(Intercept)" "phenotypeL"  "areaTZ"
> > colnames(model.matrix(~area+phenotype))
>   [1] "(Intercept)" "areaTZ"      "phenotypeL"
>
> Perhaps, I made mistakes in between?

No, you illustrated my point as well. The two coefficients of note here 
are areaTZ and phenotypeL, and the only difference between the design 
matrices is the order that they appear.

But you make a further statement above 'I want to know do the phenotypes 
(HS & LS) have effect on the area.'. This looks to me like you want the 
interaction term, which captures the difference in phenotype, given the 
area (or conversely, the differences in area, given phenotype).

I believe there is at least one example of an interaction term in the 
limma User's Guide that you can look at to gain understanding.

Best,

Jim


